<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Buffalo River (KwaZulu-Natal)</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mzinyathi River</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Buffalo River, or Mzinyathi, is a river in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kwazulu-natal">KwaZulu-Natal</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>, a major tributary of the Tugela. In the 19th century it formed part of the boundary between the British colony of Natal and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zulu-kingdom">Zulu Kingdom</a>. Rorke's Drift, scene of a famous defence in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-zulu-war">Anglo-Zulu War</a> of 1879, lies at a crossing on the river.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/buffalo-river-kwazulu-natal.jpg" alt="Buffalo River (KwaZulu-Natal)" width="320" height="208" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LL1882_pg247_RORKE%27S_DRIFT,_BUFFALO_RIVER.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
